      "the_control_of_attack_by_octopus": "The control of attack by Octopus",
      "the_control_of_attack_by_octopus_2": "The control of attack by Octopus",
      "the_cretaceous_paleogene_extinction_66": "The Cretaceous-Paleogene extinction (~66 MYA) wiped out all AMMONOID cephalopods + all BELEMNITE cephalopods. Modern cephalopods are descendants of survivors from a small subset of lineages.",
      "the_current_understanding_of_octopus_c": "The current understanding of octopus camouflage matching is that they integrate INTENSITY (chromatophores), TEXTURE (papillae), and PATTERN (uniform / mottle / disruptive) — three independent dimensions matched simultaneously in ~150 ms.",
      "the_cuttlefish_passing_cloud_display_i": "The cuttlefish \"passing cloud\" display is a wave of dark pigment that rolls down the mantle in <2 seconds. It is thought to startle or mesmerize prey by mimicking moving shadows.",
      "the_deep_ocean_under_climate_change": "The deep ocean under climate change",
      "the_deep_sea_cephalopod_world": "The deep-sea cephalopod world",
      "the_definitive_popular_science_book_on": "The definitive popular-science book on octopus biology + cognition. Co-authored by three field-leading scientists.",
      "the_devonian_nekton_revolution": "The Devonian nekton revolution",
      "the_discovery_of_social_signaling_in_o": "The discovery of social signaling in Octopus tetricus (Scheel 2017) overturned a textbook claim of strict octopus solitariness. Science textbooks now describe cephalopod sociality as VARIABLE + species-specific.",
      "the_dream_of_the_fisherman_s_wife": "\"The Dream of the Fisherman's Wife\"",
      "the_earliest_cephalopod_plectronoceras": "The earliest cephalopod (Plectronoceras, ~530 MYA) was the size of a thumb and had a chambered shell — a precursor to nautilus.",
      "the_earliest_direct_evidence_of_cephal": "The earliest direct evidence of cephalopod CAMOUFLAGE is in fossil chromatophores from a Jurassic squid (~150 MYA) preserved in unusual sediment.",
      "the_earliest_documented_ink_is_preserv": "The earliest documented INK is preserved in Jurassic-age fossil squid (~150 MYA). Some specimens still contain residual melanin pigment.",
      "the_earliest_known_octopus_a_soft_bodi": "The earliest known octopus — a soft-bodied coleoid preserved in a remarkable concretion from Illinois's Mazon Creek fossil bed. The body, arms, and even possible chromatophores are visible. Soft-bodied animals almost never fossilize.",
      "the_earliest_known_relative_of_the_mod": "The earliest known relative of the modern vampire squid. Exceptional soft-tissue preservation in the La Voulte-sur-Rhône Lagerstätte (France) preserved 8 arms with hooked attachments + eye details.",
      "the_earliest_octopus_fossil_pohlsepia_": "The earliest octopus fossil (Pohlsepia mazonensis, ~150 MYA) was preserved in unique conditions — anoxic sediment in the Mazon Creek formation, Illinois.",
      "the_eating_question": "🧭 The eating question",
      "the_edge_of_sentience_risk_and_precaut": "The Edge of Sentience: Risk and Precaution in Humans, Other Animals, and AI",
      "the_electric_sense_of_sharks_and_rays": "The electric sense of sharks and rays",
      "the_emerging_role_of_rna_editing_in_pl": "The emerging role of RNA editing in plasticity",
      "the_eu_recognized_cephalopods_as_senti": "The EU recognized cephalopods as sentient in 2010 for research purposes. The UK extended this to ALL contexts in 2022. The US still does not. What evidence would convince you a cephalopod can feel?",
      "the_evidence_for_cephalopod_sentience": "The evidence for cephalopod sentience",
      "the_eye_of_an_octopus_is_structurally_": "The eye of an octopus is structurally very similar to a vertebrate eye. This is an example of:",
      "the_first_fossil_evidence_of_cephalopo": "The first fossil evidence of cephalopod camouflage skin is from preserved fossil ammonoids — pigment cells survived in some Mesozoic shales.",
      "the_first_giant_squid_to_be_photograph": "The first GIANT SQUID to be photographed alive was recorded in 2004 by Japanese researchers Kubodera + Mori using a sperm-whale-baited camera at 900 m depth.",
      "the_first_known_cephalopod_a_small_con": "The first known cephalopod. A small cone-shaped shell from Cambrian China. The animal had tentacles + a primitive siphuncle (the tube that runs through nautilus chambers regulating buoyancy). Cephalopod blueprint already established at 2 cm.",
      "the_first_published_octopus_genome": "The first published octopus genome",
      "the_first_time_your_camo_climbs_above_": "The first time your camo % climbs above 90% while you're motionless. Suddenly the predators don't come for you.",
      "the_flip_side_targeted_fisheries_are_e": "The flip side: targeted fisheries are expanding to match the population increase. Global cephalopod catch is now ",
      "the_full_day": "📜 The full day",
