      "type_alloy_is_mostly_lead_compositors_": "Type alloy is mostly lead. Compositors picked up sorts thousands of times a day; casters worked over molten metal. Chronic low-dose lead exposure produced the \"printer's palsy\" that 19th-century occupational physicians documented. Modern letterpress shops use polymer plates or photopolymer instead.",
